{"w":2400,"h":3406,"lines":[{"c":1,"t":"Audioscripts","x":0.071929597580514343,"h":0.017975301512955122,"y":0.042611186436299908,"w":0.12830575307210287},{"t":"SUPERVISOR:","y":0.093023255904843394,"c":1,"x":0.074226806439127158,"w":0.094845358530680324,"h":0.010174418083724102},{"x":0.072086443555351487,"h":0.0093110342692153125,"t":"JOANNA:","y":0.15813518052619857,"w":0.064074535369873065,"c":1},{"h":0.0087209299460482281,"c":1,"y":0.19040697687730035,"x":0.072164949033939038,"t":"SUPERVISOR:","w":0.096907215118408205},{"y":0.22227439318721254,"h":0.0089395856829299625,"c":1,"w":0.061917063395182298,"t":"JOANNA:","x":0.072134251712933667},{"x":0.18556700231703965,"h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1,"t":"Musicians are quite vulnerable physically, aren't they, because the movements","w":0.66391754150390625,"y":0.091569767491157972},{"t":"they carry out are very intensive and repetitive, so I'd imagine some features","x":0.18138378144151668,"y":0.10680356211524622,"w":0.65374130249023443,"h":0.018105427937443186,"c":1},{"t":"of sports clothing could safeguard the players from the potentially dangerous.","x":0.18139743542342168,"h":0.017294148452409397,"c":1,"y":0.1222638065462911,"w":0.66197270711263023},{"w":0.22540687561035155,"h":0.017356424561263628,"c":1,"t":"effects of this son of thing.","x":0.18322582337918553,"y":0.13836242071268479},{"c":1,"x":0.18350514351722136,"t":"Yes, but musicians don't really consider it. They avoid clothing that obviously","y":0.15552325598053574,"w":0.64948455810546879,"h":0.015988371754420583},{"c":1,"x":0.17938144487912097,"h":0.014679976512037562,"y":0.17146212575239961,"w":0.46185567220052082,"t":"restricts their movements, but that's as far as they go."},{"y":0.18895348830495218,"h":0.013081395479068947,"c":1,"x":0.1835051498149543,"w":0.67835052490234382,"t":"Anyway, coming back to your own research, do you have any idea where you're"},{"t":"going from here?","h":0.018764358650427027,"y":0.20210037862425845,"c":1,"x":0.1807600468736732,"w":0.14982011159261072},{"t":"I was thinking of doing a study using an audience, including...","y":0.21947674423467856,"c":1,"x":0.18144329491071953,"w":0.53195877075195308,"h":0.01453488361674482},{"x":0.070103094123733029,"y":0.27180232562404982,"c":1,"t":"SECTION 4","w":0.16494845072428385,"h":0.01453488361674482},{"h":0.016889726702633556,"t":"As we saw in the last lecture, a major cause of climate change is the rapid rise in the level","x":0.072098758135606997,"y":0.29945759172049569,"w":0.76302642822265632,"c":1},{"y":0.31826189053177134,"w":0.77319585164388016,"t":"of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere over the last century. If we could reduce the amount of","x":0.070103105003913702,"h":0.013211978860833806,"c":1},{"w":0.76907216389973965,"c":1,"y":0.33284883725405412,"t":"CO2, perhaps the rate of climate change could also be slowed down. One potential method","x":0.072164948593710393,"h":0.014534883616744931},{"c":1,"t":"involves enhancing the role of the soil that plants grow in, with regard to absorbing CO2.","h":0.017615971814445075,"x":0.068041229456916694,"y":0.34879624190926284,"w":0.74845362345377597},{"y":0.36482558156114386,"w":0.74845362345377608,"c":1,"x":0.070103085133755863,"h":0.015988371754420694,"t":"Rattan Lal, a soil scientist from Ohio State University, in the USA, claims that the world's"},{"h":0.016045960131212289,"t":"agricultural soils could potentially absorb 13 per cent of the carbon dioxide in the atmosphere","y":0.38080162286586494,"x":0.068000690930061197,"c":1,"w":0.78977773030598941},{"w":0.76297643025716144,"y":0.39635830254087057,"c":1,"x":0.070061111288789654,"t":"- the equivalent of the amount released in the last 30 years. And research is going on into","h":0.015838228809224475},{"y":0.41424418609211555,"t":"how this might be achieved.","c":1,"x":0.06804124054695769,"h":0.01453488361674482,"w":0.24123710632324219},{"y":0.43746330010702761,"t":"Lal first came to the idea that soil might be valuable in this way not through an interest in","h":0.014679976512037562,"c":1,"x":0.070103103742382114,"w":0.75051544189453123},{"c":1,"x":0.067980874613279244,"w":0.76919545491536456,"y":0.45211443641874904,"h":0.017742640819538469,"t":"climate change, but rather out of concern for the land itself and the people dependent on it"},{"h":0.015999467528293398,"x":0.068041249321799363,"c":1,"w":0.77319585164388027,"t":"Carbon-rich soil is dark, crumbly and fertile, and retains some water. But erosion can occur","y":0.46946564857795337},{"c":1,"t":"if soil is dry, which is a likely effect if it contains inadequate amounts of carbon. Erosion is","h":0.014679976512037562,"w":0.75670104980468744,"x":0.068041227560602338,"y":0.48532002343366076},{"h":0.013226488374361689,"x":0.072164955837561801,"t":"of course bad for people trying to grow crops or breed animals on that terrain. In the 1970s","c":1,"y":0.50145348830243497,"w":0.76701029459635417},{"x":0.068041239373480944,"y":0.51732237202122755,"c":1,"h":0.017615971814445075,"w":0.76082473754882818,"t":"and '80s, Lal was studying soils in Africa so devoid of organic matter that the ground has"},{"x":0.070035134156122378,"h":0.017280848531672666,"w":0.78363566080729175,"y":0.53340787048126159,"t":"gecome extremely hard, like cement. There he met a pioneer in the study of global warming,","c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.013211978860833806,"x":0.070103089533134266,"w":0.78556701660156247,"t":"who suggested that carbon from the soil had moved into the atmosphere. This is now looking","y":0.5507927184693846},{"t":"increasingly likely.","x":0.068041234364863576,"y":0.56686046515645794,"c":1,"h":0.01453488361674482,"w":0.1546391805013021},{"y":0.59011627923494803,"w":0.75257731119791671,"h":0.015988371754420694,"t":"Let me explain. For millions of years, carbon dioxide levels in the atmosphere have been","x":0.068041241169561131,"c":1},{"y":0.60598943021940066,"t":"regulated, in part, by a natural partnership between plants and microbes - tiny organisms in","x":0.068041235708928227,"w":0.77731959025065112,"c":1,"h":0.014679976512037562},{"w":0.77962198893229173,"t":"the soil. Plants absorb CO2 from the air and transform it into sugars and other carbon-based","x":0.067917237316255138,"y":0.6195133650518897,"h":0.020329843320639363,"c":1},{"x":0.0679822425679356,"c":1,"w":0.7733137003580729,"h":0.017531171519827748,"t":"substances. While a proportion of these carbon products remain in the plant, some transfer","y":0.63801557251588259},{"y":0.65382944675569543,"t":"from the roots to fungl and soil microbes, which store the carbon in the soil.","w":0.63927973429361973,"c":1,"x":0.06797916343861217,"h":0.017152094099007864},{"x":0.068041236220542867,"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.67877906981746405,"t":"The invention of agriculture some 10,000 years ago disrupted these ancient soil-building","w":0.74639175415039061,"c":1},{"t":"processes and led to the loss of carbon from the soil. When humans started draining the","y":0.69335662598130687,"h":0.017492923187775511,"x":0.065937001850155455,"w":0.75060567220052077,"c":1},{"h":0.015988371754420583,"y":0.7107558141194863,"w":0.76907216389973954,"t":"natural topsoil, and ploughing it up for planting, they exposed the buried carbon to oxygen.","c":1,"x":0.065979381853913138},{"c":1,"t":"This created carbon dioxide and released it into the air. And in some places, grazing by","w":0.73834203084309891,"x":0.065895362033270052,"h":0.018168378282279352,"y":0.72460687782611044},{"w":0.74020619710286462,"y":0.74273255818943207,"t":"domesticated animals has removed all vegetation, releasing carbon into the air. Tons of","h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1,"x":0.068041231251102938},{"c":1,"t":"carbon have been stripped from the world's soils - where it's needed - and pumped into the","w":0.77938145955403648,"y":0.75866118635984214,"x":0.06804122896513462,"h":0.013211978860833806},{"w":0.10977321624755858,"y":0.77548793017665152,"t":"atmosphere.","x":0.067892072842609827,"h":0.012559466269600139,"c":1},{"t":"So what can be done? Researchers are now coming up with evidence that even modest","y":0.79941860458423497,"h":0.013081395479069058,"c":1,"x":0.068041229407132559,"w":0.74845362345377608},{"h":0.013211978860833806,"w":0.78144327799479163,"x":0.068041247507267907,"c":1,"y":0.8153258953202126,"t":"changes to farming can significantly help to reduce the amount of carbon in the atmosphere."},{"t":"Some growers have already started using an approach known as regenerative agriculture.","x":0.070103116094555273,"h":0.014679976512037562,"w":0.76288655598958344,"c":1,"y":0.83852025847696443},{"w":0.77329055786132816,"t":"This aims to boost the fertility of soil and keep it moist through established practices. These","c":1,"x":0.065931813775549505,"y":0.85454228115147113,"h":0.016088851955590733},{"x":0.063783341104924229,"t":"include keeping fields planted all year round, and increasing the variety of plants being.","y":0.86763422078048869,"c":1,"w":0.74462666829427082,"h":0.02194986438583213},{"x":0.067981942722607491,"c":1,"y":0.88658583789735168,"t":"grown. Strategies like these can significantly increase the amount of carbon stored in the soil,","h":0.016637111088141809,"w":0.79390553792317708},{"x":0.068041232028610732,"w":0.79381444295247405,"h":0.013211978860833806,"c":1,"t":"so agricultural researchers are now building a case for their use in combating climate change.","y":0.9039929537525826},{"t":"122","y":0.9520348836013085,"w":0.037113402684529631,"x":0.063917525410312495,"h":0.013081395479068947,"c":1},{"t":"leltsresources.org","x":0.35206821434163693,"h":0.02519279833898358,"c":1,"w":0.29379859924316409,"y":0.95184192158160008},{"y":0.10755813943129311,"h":0.013081395479069058,"t":"Q30","x":0.8762886605100294,"w":0.039175256093343158,"c":1},{"y":0.46947674395741323,"t":"Q31","x":0.87422680401856001,"w":0.037113402684529673,"h":0.013081395479068947,"c":1},{"x":0.87422680401856001,"w":0.037113402684529673,"y":0.51744186033552297,"h":0.01453488361674482,"t":"Q32","c":1},{"t":"Q33","w":0.037113402684529673,"x":0.87422680370928141,"h":0.011627907341393073,"y":0.62209302304118985,"c":1},{"t":"Q34","c":1,"w":0.039175256093343158,"h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.87422680483419901,"y":0.63808139524738416},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395479069058,"t":"Q35","y":0.85465116268470231,"w":0.039175256093343158,"x":0.87216494917626652},{"x":0.8701030930469722,"t":"Q36","c":1,"h":0.013081395479068947,"w":0.041237112681070887,"y":0.87063953478013034}]}